Subject: [PATCH 2/2] P8 round 3b: evidence quality gates human resolution;
 persistent uniqueness uncertainty

- reconcile() reports evidence: POSITIVE / NEGATIVE_COMPLETE (structured 404
  AND complete bounded scan) / INCOMPLETE. force_scan for human checks.
- abandon() and release_entry_lock() require a persisted NEGATIVE_COMPLETE
  fresh check; unavailable, failed, truncated, bounded or stuck evidence is
  refused. Lock, history and monitoring preserved. NEGATIVE_COMPLETE is not
  proof of absence; human-resolution policy remains unapproved.
- New ACCEPTED_UNVERIFIED: order known but uniqueness unconfirmed; monitored,
  entries locked, re-scanned every cycle, survives restart; not abandonable.
- History events recorded only on real state changes.

Tests: round3b 19 (13 fail on 83ef87c; 19 pass); round3 21, round2 15,
existing 30 all pass unchanged (85/85). Codex reproduction (verbatim) now:
abandon/release refused, lock held.
Round-4 timeout hardening and paper-plan corrections remain OPEN.
